IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-interpretation-time`

-- Part 6 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): functions and powers (sections 37 to 43).
-- Each function answers one question about one subsection.
-- A question is asked of a situation described by the inputs; the Act or instrument that confers the function is the setting, not an input.
-- Section 38 compares moments, so this module imports the time module for `Moment`.

§ `Part 6 -- Functions and powers (sections 37 to 43)`

§§ `37 -- Performance of functions`

-- src:445 | (1) If an Act or a legislative instrument confers a function on a person or body, the function may be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref s 37(1) (src:445)
`a function conferred on a person or body may be performed from time to time as occasion requires` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:446 | (2) If an Act or a legislative instrument confers a function on the holder of a particular office, the function may be performed by the person for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office.
@ref s 37(2) (src:446)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being holding the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is for the time being performing the duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a function conferred on the holder of an office may be performed by the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is for the time being holding the office` OR `the person is for the time being performing the duties of the office`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:447 | (3) If an Act or a legislative instrument confers a function on a body, the performance of the function is not affected merely because of a vacancy in the membership of the body or a defect in the appointment of a member.
@ref s 37(3) (src:447)
GIVEN `the only ground is a vacancy in the membership of the body or a flaw in the appointment of a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the performance of a function conferred on a body is affected` MEANS
    IF `the only ground is a vacancy in the membership of the body or a flaw in the appointment of a member` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `38 -- Performance of functions under provision before commencement`

-- src:449 | (1) If—
-- src:450 | (a) a provision of an Act that has passed, or a legislative instrument that has been made, is not yet in operation; and
-- src:451 | (b) it is expedient that a function conferred on a person or body by the provision be performed before it comes into operation,
-- src:452 | the function may be so performed before the provision comes into operation.
@ref s 38(1) (src:449-452)
GIVEN `the provision of an Act has passed, or the legislative instrument has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is not yet in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is expedient that a function conferred on a person or body by the provision be performed before it comes into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a function conferred by a provision not yet in operation may be performed before it comes into operation` MEANS
    IF `the provision of an Act has passed, or the legislative instrument has been made`
       AND `the provision is not yet in operation`
       AND `it is expedient that a function conferred on a person or body by the provision be performed before it comes into operation`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Subsection (2) says a thing done by virtue of subsection (1) takes effect when the provision comes into operation and not before.
-- Subsection (3)(b) says the same of a function performed by an appointee or an established body.
-- src:453 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), anything created, granted, issued, done or made under or pursuant to a provision by virtue of subsection (1) will take effect when the provision comes into operation and not before.
@ref s 38(2) (src:453)
GIVEN `the moment asked about` IS A Moment
      `the moment the provision comes into operation` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a thing done by virtue of section 38(1) has taken effect` MEANS
    `s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment asked about`
        AT LEAST `s 4: the position of a moment in seconds` `the moment the provision comes into operation`

-- src:454 | (3) If the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body—
-- src:455 | (a) the appointed person may act in the office or the established body may meet and perform its functions with the same entitlement to remuneration or allowances as if the provision were in operation; but
-- src:456 | (b) any function performed by that person or body pursuant to subsection (1) does not take effect until the relevant provision comes into operation.
@ref s 38(3) (src:454-456)
GIVEN `the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointed person may act in the office or the established body may meet and perform its functions before the provision comes into operation` MEANS
    IF `the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:454 | (3) If the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body—
-- src:455 | (a) the appointed person may act in the office or the established body may meet and perform its functions with the same entitlement to remuneration or allowances as if the provision were in operation; but
-- src:456 | (b) any function performed by that person or body pursuant to subsection (1) does not take effect until the relevant provision comes into operation.
@ref s 38(3) (src:454-456)
GIVEN `the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointed person or the established body has the same entitlement to remuneration or allowances as if the provision were in operation` MEANS
    IF `the function that is performed is the appointment of a person to a specified office or the establishment of a specified body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `39 -- Certain meetings etc may occur remotely`

DECLARE `Requirement of physical presence` IS ONE OF
    `a requirement that a meeting occur or that some other transaction take place that requires 2 or more persons to be physically present`
    `a requirement that a person be physically present to witness the signing, execution, certification or stamping of a document or to take any oath, affirmation or declaration in relation to a document`
    `another requirement`

DECLARE `Means of remote communication` IS ONE OF
    `audio visual`
    `audio`
    `audio visual and audio together`
    `another means`

-- src:458 | (1) If an Act or a legislative instrument requires that a meeting occur or that some other transaction take place that requires 2 or more persons to be physically present, the requirement will be taken to be satisfied if the persons meet, or the transaction takes place, remotely using 1 or both (including a combination) of the following means of communication:
-- src:459 | (a) audio visual;
-- src:460 | (b) audio.
-- src:461 | (2) However, subsection (1) does not apply to a requirement that a person be physically present to witness the signing, execution, certification or stamping of a document or to take any oath, affirmation or declaration in relation to a document.
-- src:462 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a meeting or transaction, or meeting or transaction of a class, prescribed by the regulations.
@ref s 39(1)-(3) (src:458-462)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of physical presence`
      means IS A `Means of remote communication`
      `the meeting or transaction, or its class, is prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the requirement is taken to be satisfied by meeting or transacting remotely` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
        WHEN `a requirement that a meeting occur or that some other transaction take place that requires 2 or more persons to be physically present` THEN
            IF `the meeting or transaction, or its class, is prescribed by the regulations` THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE (CONSIDER means
                    WHEN `audio visual` THEN JUST TRUE
                    WHEN `audio` THEN JUST TRUE
                    WHEN `audio visual and audio together` THEN JUST TRUE
                    WHEN `another means` THEN JUST FALSE)
        WHEN `a requirement that a person be physically present to witness the signing, execution, certification or stamping of a document or to take any oath, affirmation or declaration in relation to a document` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `another requirement` THEN NOTHING

-- src:463 | (4) A person who participates in a meeting in accordance with this section is taken to be present at the meeting, and to form part of any quorum for the meeting, even if the person is not physically present at the same place as another person participating in the meeting.
@ref s 39(4) (src:463)
GIVEN `the person participates in a meeting in accordance with section 39` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is taken to be present at the meeting and to form part of any quorum` MEANS
    IF `the person participates in a meeting in accordance with section 39` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `40 -- Power to make instrument includes power to amend or repeal`

-- src:465 | A power under an Act or a legislative instrument to make an instrument (including a legislative instrument) includes a power to amend or repeal the instrument in the same way, and subject to the same conditions if appropriate for that purpose, as it was made.
@ref s 40 (src:465)
GIVEN `the amendment or repeal is made in the same way as the instrument was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a power to make an instrument includes a power to amend or repeal it` MEANS
    IF `the amendment or repeal is made in the same way as the instrument was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:465 | A power under an Act or a legislative instrument to make an instrument (including a legislative instrument) includes a power to amend or repeal the instrument in the same way, and subject to the same conditions if appropriate for that purpose, as it was made.
@ref s 40 (src:465)
GIVEN `it is appropriate for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the same conditions apply to the amendment or repeal as applied to the making` MEANS
    IF `it is appropriate for that purpose` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `41 -- Powers of appointment`

-- src:467 | (1) This section applies if an Act or a legislative instrument authorises or requires a person (the appointer)—
-- src:468 | (a) to appoint a person to an office or to act in an office; or
-- src:469 | (b) to appoint a person to perform a function or do any other thing,
-- src:470 | and any form of authorisation to perform a function or do a thing is taken to be an appointment for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 41(1) (src:467-470)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument authorises or requires a person to appoint a person to an office or to act in an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or instrument authorises or requires a person to appoint a person to perform a function or do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is a form of authorisation to perform a function or do a thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 41 applies` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument authorises or requires a person to appoint a person to an office or to act in an office`
       OR `the Act or instrument authorises or requires a person to appoint a person to perform a function or do any other thing`
       OR `the authorisation is a form of authorisation to perform a function or do a thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Thing an appointer may do` IS ONE OF
    `appoint a person by name or by reference to the title of an office held by a person`
    `determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances (if any)`
    `terminate or suspend an appointment`
    `reinstate or reappoint a person whose appointment has been terminated or suspended`
    `appoint another person, temporarily or permanently, in the cases in paragraph (e)`
    `something else an appointer may do`

-- src:471 | (2) The appointer may (in the appointer's discretion) do any of the following:
-- src:472 | (a) appoint a person by name or by reference to the title of an office held by a person;
-- src:473 | (b) determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances (if any);
-- src:474 | (c) terminate or suspend an appointment;
-- src:475 | (d) reinstate or reappoint a person whose appointment has been terminated or suspended;
-- src:476 | (e) appoint another person, temporarily or permanently—
@ref s 41(2) (src:471-476)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing an appointer may do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointer may do this in the appointer's discretion` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `appoint a person by name or by reference to the title of an office held by a person` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `determine the terms and conditions of the appointment, including remuneration and allowances (if any)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `terminate or suspend an appointment` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reinstate or reappoint a person whose appointment has been terminated or suspended` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `appoint another person, temporarily or permanently, in the cases in paragraph (e)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `something else an appointer may do` THEN NOTHING

-- src:476 | (e) appoint another person, temporarily or permanently—
-- src:477 | (i) if the person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position; or
-- src:478 | (ii) if the office or position is vacant (including where the previous appointment has been terminated or suspended).
@ref s 41(2)(e) (src:476-478)
GIVEN `the person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office or position is vacant (including where the previous appointment has been terminated or suspended)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointer may appoint another person temporarily or permanently` MEANS
    IF `the person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position`
       OR `the office or position is vacant (including where the previous appointment has been terminated or suspended)`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:479 | (3) An authorisation or requirement in an Act or a legislative instrument to appoint a person to an office will be taken to include an authorisation to appoint a person to act in the office.
@ref s 41(3) (src:479)
GIVEN `the authorisation or requirement is to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is taken to include an authorisation to appoint a person to act in the office` MEANS
    IF `the authorisation or requirement is to appoint a person to an office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:480 | (4) A person may be appointed to act in an office (whether pursuant to a specific authorisation or requirement in an Act or a legislative instrument or pursuant to subsection (3)) even if no appointment has ever been made to the office.
@ref s 41(4) (src:480)
GIVEN `the appointment to act is made pursuant to a specific authorisation or requirement, or pursuant to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no appointment has ever been made to the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person may be appointed to act in the office` MEANS
    IF `the appointment to act is made pursuant to a specific authorisation or requirement, or pursuant to subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:481 | (5) If the holder of a particular office is appointed to do a thing, the person for the time being holding or performing the duties of that office is taken to be appointed to do that thing.
@ref s 41(5) (src:481)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is taken to be appointed to do the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person is for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:482 | (6) A person appointed to act in an office has all the functions of the holder of the office.
@ref s 41(6) (src:482)
GIVEN `the person is appointed to act in the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person has all the functions of the holder of the office` MEANS
    IF `the person is appointed to act in the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:483 | (7) An appointment made by the holder of a particular office does not cease to have effect merely because the appointer ceases to hold that office.
@ref s 41(7) (src:483)
GIVEN `the only ground is that the appointer ceases to hold the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an appointment made by the holder of a particular office ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the only ground is that the appointer ceases to hold the office` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Ground for challenging what a person purporting to act did` IS ONE OF
    `the occasion for the appointment had not arisen`
    `there was a flaw or irregularity in connection with the appointment`
    `the appointment had ceased to have effect`
    `the occasion for the person to act had not arisen or had ceased`
    `another ground`

-- src:484 | (8) Anything done by, or in relation to, a person purporting to act in an office pursuant to an appointment is not invalid merely because—
-- src:485 | (a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen; or
-- src:486 | (b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the appointment; or
-- src:487 | (c) the appointment had ceased to have effect; or
-- src:488 | (d) the occasion for the person to act had not arisen or had ceased.
@ref s 41(8) (src:484-488)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground for challenging what a person purporting to act did`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what was done by a person purporting to act in an office is invalid merely because` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
        WHEN `the occasion for the appointment had not arisen` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `there was a flaw or irregularity in connection with the appointment` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `the appointment had ceased to have effect` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `the occasion for the person to act had not arisen or had ceased` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `another ground` THEN NOTHING

§§ `42 -- Gender balance in nomination of persons for appointment to statutory bodies`

-- src:490 | (1) This section applies if an Act or a legislative instrument provides for a member of a body to be appointed by the Governor or a Minister on the nomination of a non‑government entity.
@ref s 42(1) (src:490)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument provides for a member of a body to be appointed by the Governor or a Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is on the nomination of a non-government entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 42 applies` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument provides for a member of a body to be appointed by the Governor or a Minister`
       AND `the appointment is on the nomination of a non-government entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Section 42(5): "non-government entity means a person or body other than an officer, agency or instrumentality ... of the Crown".
-- src:501 | (5) In this section—
-- src:503 | non-government entity means a person or body other than an officer, agency or instrumentality (including a Minister) of the Crown in right of the State or the Commonwealth or another State or a Territory of the Commonwealth;
@ref s 42(5) non-government entity (src:501-503)
GIVEN `the person or body is an officer, agency or instrumentality (including a Minister) of the Crown in right of the State or the Commonwealth or another State or a Territory of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person or body is a non-government entity` MEANS
    NOT `the person or body is an officer, agency or instrumentality (including a Minister) of the Crown in right of the State or the Commonwealth or another State or a Territory of the Commonwealth`

-- src:502 | man includes a person who identifies himself as a man regardless of the person's designated sex at birth;
@ref s 42(5) man (src:502)
GIVEN `the person identifies himself as a man` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is a man for section 42 regardless of the person's designated sex at birth` MEANS
    IF `the person identifies himself as a man` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:504 | woman includes a person who identifies herself as a woman regardless of the person's designated sex at birth.
@ref s 42(5) woman (src:504)
GIVEN `the person identifies herself as a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person is a woman for section 42 regardless of the person's designated sex at birth` MEANS
    IF `the person identifies herself as a woman` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 42(2)(a) and (3)(b)(i): "must include at least 1 woman and 1 man".
-- src:491 | (2) If the Act provides for the non‑government entity to nominate a panel of persons from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person for appointment, the Act will be taken to provide that the panel—
-- src:492 | (a) must include at least 1 woman and 1 man; and
-- src:496 | (b) the panel—
-- src:497 | (i) must include at least 1 woman and 1 man; and
@ref s 42(2)(a) and (3)(b)(i) (src:491-497)
GIVEN `the number of women on the panel` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of men on the panel` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the panel includes at least 1 woman and 1 man` MEANS
    `the number of women on the panel` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of men on the panel` AT LEAST 1

-- Section 42(2)(b) and (3)(b)(ii): "must, as far as practicable, be comprised of equal numbers of women and men".
-- Where equal numbers are not practicable the text does not say how far from equal the panel may be.
-- src:493 | (b) must, as far as practicable, be comprised of equal numbers of women and men.
-- src:498 | (ii) must, as far as practicable, be comprised of equal numbers of women and men; and
@ref s 42(2)(b) and (3)(b)(ii) (src:493-498)
GIVEN `the number of women on the panel` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of men on the panel` IS A NUMBER
      `equal numbers are practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the panel is comprised of equal numbers of women and men as far as practicable` MEANS
    IF `equal numbers are practicable`
    THEN JUST (`the number of women on the panel` EQUALS `the number of men on the panel`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 42(3)(a): "not less than twice the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity plus 1".
-- src:494 | (3) If the Act does not provide for the non‑government entity to nominate a panel of persons from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person for appointment, the Act will be taken to provide that—
-- src:495 | (a) the non‑government entity must nominate a panel of persons comprised of not less than twice the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity plus 1; and
@ref s 42(3)(a) (src:494-495)
GIVEN `the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fewest persons the panel may comprise` MEANS
    (2 TIMES `the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity`) PLUS 1

-- The other reading of the same words: twice the number with 1 added to the number before doubling.
-- src:495 | (a) the non‑government entity must nominate a panel of persons comprised of not less than twice the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity plus 1; and
@ref s 42(3)(a) (src:495)
GIVEN `the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fewest persons the panel may comprise on the reading that doubles the number plus 1` MEANS
    2 TIMES (`the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity` PLUS 1)

-- src:495 | (a) the non‑government entity must nominate a panel of persons comprised of not less than twice the number of members of the body to be appointed on the nomination of the entity plus 1; and
@ref s 42(3)(a) (src:495)
GIVEN `the Act provides for the non-government entity to nominate a panel from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Act is taken to provide that the non-government entity must nominate a panel` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for the non-government entity to nominate a panel from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:499 | (c) the Governor or Minister must select the person for appointment from the panel.
@ref s 42(3)(c) (src:499)
GIVEN `the Act provides for the non-government entity to nominate a panel from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Act is taken to provide that the Governor or Minister must select the person from the panel` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for the non-government entity to nominate a panel from which the Governor or Minister is to select a person` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:500 | (4) This section does not derogate from the need to properly assess merit in selecting persons for appointment.
@ref s 42(4) (src:500)
`section 42 derogates from the need to properly assess merit in selecting persons for appointment` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `43 -- Powers of delegation`

-- src:506 | (1) This section applies if an Act or a legislative instrument authorises a person or body to delegate a function.
@ref s 43(1) (src:506)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument authorises a person or body to delegate a function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 43 applies` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument authorises a person or body to delegate a function` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:507 | (2) A delegation may be made subject to conditions or limitations specified by the delegator and may be revoked at any time by the delegator.
@ref s 43(2) (src:507)
`a delegation may be made subject to conditions or limitations specified by the delegator` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:507 | (2) A delegation may be made subject to conditions or limitations specified by the delegator and may be revoked at any time by the delegator.
@ref s 43(2) (src:507)
`a delegation may be revoked at any time by the delegator` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:508 | (3) Unless the Act or the legislative instrument expressly provides to the contrary, a delegation of the power of delegation cannot be made (and any purported delegation of all of the functions of the delegator will be read as if the delegation referred to all of the functions of the delegator other than the power of delegation).
@ref s 43(3) (src:508)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument expressly provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a delegation of the power of delegation can be made` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument expressly provides to the contrary` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:508 | (3) Unless the Act or the legislative instrument expressly provides to the contrary, a delegation of the power of delegation cannot be made (and any purported delegation of all of the functions of the delegator will be read as if the delegation referred to all of the functions of the delegator other than the power of delegation).
@ref s 43(3) (src:508)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument expressly provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a purported delegation of all of the functions of the delegator is read as excluding the power of delegation` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument expressly provides to the contrary` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:509 | (4) If a function, when exercised by a delegator, is dependent on the delegator's opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter, the function, when exercised by a delegate, is dependent on the delegate's opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to that matter.
@ref s 43(4) (src:509)
GIVEN `the function, when exercised by the delegator, is dependent on the delegator's opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 43(4) makes the function depend on the delegate's opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to that matter` MEANS
    IF `the function, when exercised by the delegator, is dependent on the delegator's opinion, belief or state of mind in relation to a matter` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:510 | (5) A function that has been delegated, when exercised by a delegate, will be taken to have been exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 43(5) (src:510)
GIVEN `the function has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is exercised by the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the function is taken to have been exercised by the delegator` MEANS
    IF `the function has been delegated` AND `it is exercised by the delegate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:511 | (6) A function that has been delegated may, despite the delegation, be exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 43(6) (src:511)
GIVEN `the function has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegator may exercise the function despite the delegation` MEANS
    IF `the function has been delegated` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Way of naming a delegate` IS ONE OF
    `by name`
    `by reference to the title of an office held by a person or body`
    `another way of naming a delegate`

-- src:512 | (7) The delegator may delegate the function to a person or body by name or by reference to the title of an office held by a person or body.
@ref s 43(7) (src:512)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of naming a delegate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegator may delegate the function to a person or body in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
        WHEN `by name` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `by reference to the title of an office held by a person or body` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another way of naming a delegate` THEN NOTHING

-- src:513 | (8) A delegation made to the holder of a particular office will be taken to be made to the person for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office.
@ref s 43(8) (src:513)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation to the holder of a particular office is taken to be made to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is for the time being holding or performing the duties of the office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:514 | (9) A delegation of all the functions of a person or body under an Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, includes any additional function given to the delegator under the Act, instrument or provision by an amendment made to it after the delegation has taken effect.
@ref s 43(9) (src:514)
GIVEN `the delegation is of all the functions of a person or body under an Act or instrument or a provision of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional function was given to the delegator by an amendment made after the delegation has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation includes the additional function` MEANS
    IF `the delegation is of all the functions of a person or body under an Act or instrument or a provision of one`
       AND `the additional function was given to the delegator by an amendment made after the delegation has taken effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:515 | (10) If a function of a person or body under an Act or a legislative instrument is delegated and, after the delegation has taken effect, the scope of that function is altered by an amendment made to the Act or the instrument, the delegation is of the function as so altered.
@ref s 43(10) (src:515)
GIVEN `the function is delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scope of the function is altered by an amendment made after the delegation has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delegation is of the function as so altered` MEANS
    IF `the function is delegated` AND `the scope of the function is altered by an amendment made after the delegation has taken effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:516 | (11) A delegation made by, or to, the holder of a particular office does not cease to have effect merely because the person who held the office when the function was delegated ceases to do so.
@ref s 43(11) (src:516)
GIVEN `the only ground is that the person who held the office when the function was delegated ceases to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a delegation made by, or to, the holder of a particular office ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the only ground is that the person who held the office when the function was delegated ceases to do so` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:517 | (12) The validity of a delegation is not affected by a grammatical error, spelling error, error of punctuation, formatting error or other minor error if the scope and meaning of the delegation is readily apparent despite the error.
@ref s 43(12) (src:517)
GIVEN `the error is a grammatical error, spelling error, error of punctuation, formatting error or other minor error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scope and meaning of the delegation is readily apparent despite the error` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the validity of a delegation is affected by the error` MEANS
    IF `the error is a grammatical error, spelling error, error of punctuation, formatting error or other minor error`
       AND `the scope and meaning of the delegation is readily apparent despite the error`
    THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:518 | (13) In this section—
-- src:519 | delegate includes sub‑delegate.
@ref s 43(13) (src:518-519)
GIVEN `the person or body is a sub-delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person or body is a delegate within section 43` MEANS
    IF `the person or body is a sub-delegate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

